---
id: journey_derelict
title: Ghost Ship
tags: [discovery, salvage]
context: journey
weight: 9
cooldown: 5
---

=== intro

Your sensors paint a vessel drifting in the void. No drive signature. No 
running lights. No response to standard hails.

The hull configuration is old—pre-Cataclysm old. A human-era design, 
abandoned here for over a century.

Ghost ships happen. But they never stop being unsettling.

* [Board and investigate]
  ~ fuel -= 3
  -> board

* [Scan remotely and move on]
  -> scan

* [Leave it alone]
  ~ chronicle "Ghost Ship"
    Detected a pre-Cataclysm derelict. Chose not to investigate.
  -> END

=== board

Your docking systems interface with the ancient vessel. The seals are 
corroded but hold. Inside: darkness, silence, the smell of long-dead 
atmosphere.

The crew quarters are empty. Whatever happened here, it happened fast.

In the engineering section, you find a functional memory core. Old 
data—personnel records, navigation logs, final communications.

* [Take the memory core]
  ~ addCard cargo_memory_crystal
  ~ flag derelict_salvaged
  ~ chronicle "Derelict Salvage"
    Boarded a Cataclysm-era derelict. Salvaged a memory core from engineering.
  -> END

* [Leave everything as it was]
  ~ integrity += 3
  ~ chronicle "Ghost Ship"
    Boarded a Cataclysm-era derelict. Left the remains undisturbed.
  -> END

=== scan

Your sensors sweep the derelict. Hull integrity: 23%. Power reserves: depleted. 
Life signs: none—but that's expected.

Wait. There's something in the cargo bay. Low-level EM signature. Could be 
salvageable equipment. Could be something else.

* [Closer inspection isn't worth the risk]
  ~ chronicle "Ghost Ship"
    Scanned a pre-Cataclysm derelict. Something was active in the cargo bay. Didn't investigate.
  -> END

* [Board to investigate the signature]
  ~ fuel -= 3
  -> board
